in health news new research on the  psychological impact of the coronavirus  english scientists found people  diagnosed with covid19 are at a greater  risk of developing a range of  psychological and neurological  conditions  now one man says he wasn't too concerned  when he was diagnosed and eventually  recovered but  things changed very quickly it instantly  like a light switch  i felt this intense paranoia hit me i  couldn't  escape it it kept every single person  that i saw would trigger  this this intense fear and and how bad  did it get  as i was hearing voices outside the  window you know i thought i heard people  in the bushes  doctors were able to link that man's  condition to coronavirus and found out  that he's not alone  oxford researchers say one in three  covid patients in the u.s developed  brain or psychiatric disorders within  six  months of being infected some disorders  were common like anxiety or depression  however some patients developed  psychosis and dementia  they hope future studies will reveal  more about how covet interacts with the  brain
 

